IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Parliamentary Privileges Act 1987 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE
-- TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03430.txt
-- (compilation No. 4, 21 October 2016). The person dealing with Parliament
-- asks: "Can a House punish me for this, and how far; is it a crime under this
-- Act; am I immune from court and civil arrest on this day?"

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `a natural person`
    `a corporation`

-- s 14: the capacity in which I claim immunity.
DECLARE `My role` IS ONE OF
    `a member of a House`
    `an officer of a House`
    `a person required to attend before a House or committee`
    `none of these`

-- ss 12-13: the conduct the Act makes an offence.
DECLARE `Statutory conduct` IS ONE OF
    `improperly influencing a witness's evidence, or inducing them not to give it`
    `penalising or injuring a person on account of evidence`
    `publishing or disclosing in camera evidence without authority`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `Privileges case` HAS
    `I am`                                                          IS A `Kind of person`
    -- ss 4, 6: conduct said to be an offence against a House
    `my conduct improperly interferes, or is intended or likely to` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is only defamatory or critical of Parliament, a House, a committee or a member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was in the presence of a House or committee`                IS A BOOLEAN
    -- ss 12-13
    `what I do`                                                     IS A `Statutory conduct`
    `a House or committee has published or authorised the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 14
    `my role`                                                       IS A `My role`
    `the day asked about`                                           IS A DATE
    -- for a member: the days my House, or a committee of which I am a member,
    -- meets; for an officer: the days a House or committee I must attend
    -- meets; for a witness: the days I am required to attend
    `the sitting days`                                              IS A LIST OF DATE

DECLARE `Privileges position` HAS
    `a House may punish my conduct`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `most imprisonment a House may impose, in months`               IS A NUMBER
    `most fine a House may impose, in dollars`                      IS A NUMBER
    `I commit an offence against this Act`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `most imprisonment for that offence, in months`                 IS A NUMBER
    `most penalty units for that offence`                           IS A NUMBER
    `I am immune from court attendance and civil arrest that day`   IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

-- s 4: an offence against a House requires conduct that amounts, or is
-- intended or likely to amount, to an improper interference. s 6: not by reason
-- only that it is defamatory or critical, except in the presence of a House or
-- committee.
@ref ss 4, 6
GIVEN c IS A `Privileges case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a House may punish` c IF
        c's `my conduct improperly interferes, or is intended or likely to`
    AND (   NOT (c's `it is only defamatory or critical of Parliament, a House, a committee or a member`)
         OR c's `it was in the presence of a House or committee`)

-- s 7(1): imprisonment up to 6 months; s 7(5): a fine up to $5,000 for a
-- natural person, $25,000 for a corporation; s 7(7): not both.
@ref s 7(1), (5), (7)
GIVEN c IS A `Privileges case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the House's maximum months for` c MEANS
    IF `a House may punish` c AND c's `I am` EQUALS `a natural person` THEN 6 ELSE 0

@ref s 7(5)
GIVEN c IS A `Privileges case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the House's maximum fine for` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a House may punish` c) THEN 0
        IF c's `I am` EQUALS `a natural person` THEN 5000
        OTHERWISE 25000

-- s 12(1)-(2); s 13, unless a House or committee has published or authorised
-- publication of the document or evidence.
@ref ss 12-13
GIVEN c IS A `Privileges case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I commit a statutory offence` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `what I do`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `publishing or disclosing in camera evidence without authority` THEN
        NOT (c's `a House or committee has published or authorised the evidence`)
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- ss 12-13 penalties: a natural person, imprisonment for 6 months or 50
-- penalty units; a corporation, 250 penalty units.
@ref ss 12-13 penalties
GIVEN c IS A `Privileges case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the statutory maximum months for` c MEANS
    IF `I commit a statutory offence` c AND c's `I am` EQUALS `a natural person` THEN 6 ELSE 0

GIVEN c IS A `Privileges case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the statutory maximum units for` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`I commit a statutory offence` c) THEN 0
        IF c's `I am` EQUALS `a natural person` THEN 50
        OTHERWISE 250

-- s 14(1)-(2): a member or officer, on a sitting day or within 5 days before
-- or after one; s 14(3): a person required to attend, on that day only.
@ref s 14
GIVEN c IS A `Privileges case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am immune that day` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `my role`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a person required to attend before a House or committee` THEN
        elem (c's `the day asked about`) (c's `the sitting days`)
    OTHERWISE
        any (GIVEN s YIELD `within 5 days of` (c's `the day asked about`) s) (c's `the sitting days`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE, s IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within 5 days of` d s IF
        d AT LEAST s MINUS 5
    AND d AT MOST s PLUS 5

@ref ss 4, 6, 7, 12-14
@export default The position of a person dealing with the Commonwealth Parliament under the Parliamentary Privileges Act 1987 (Cth): whether a House may punish their conduct as an offence against it (only an improper interference with a House, committee or member, and not merely for defamation or criticism outside the House's presence: ss 4, 6) and the most it may impose (6 months' imprisonment, or a fine of $5,000, or $25,000 for a corporation: s 7); whether they commit an offence under the Act by interfering with a witness or disclosing in camera evidence (ss 12-13: 6 months or 50 penalty units, or 250 penalty units for a corporation); and whether, as a member, officer or witness, they are immune that day from being required to attend a court or tribunal or arrested in a civil cause (s 14). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Privileges case`  @desc Who I am, my conduct, my role and the day asked about, and the sitting days
GIVETH A `Privileges position`
`the privileges position for` c MEANS
    `Privileges position` OF `a House may punish` c, `the House's maximum months for` c, `the House's maximum fine for` c,
                             `I commit a statutory offence` c, `the statutory maximum months for` c, `the statutory maximum units for` c,
                             `I am immune that day` c
